 "text": "**Digest 2026-10-14 UTC** · #cd-tracker (dev, 224 tickets) · since 2026-10-14\n\n**Summary**\n• AUD-37 (AB-05): MATMCD and Vashishtha resumed and finished, so all five systems run end to end. On the probe scenario both hybrids end exactly at their own data-only PC graph (F1 0.407).\n• AUD-38 / RQ-17 done: the lost Causal-Copilot run was redone; on gpt-4o-mini without names it ends below plain PC in 9 of 10 families; name reliance 0.094 (gpt-4o 0.167).\n• AUD-38 amendment 1: tier A was stopped by a machine restart after 14 runs (12 ok). Vashishtha ties 85-93% of pairs on small scenarios, each a gpt-4o call, so its tier-A runs are cut to five scenarios (tier A now 80 runs, about $48; $7.92 spent). Spend is now read from the call logs, and cap hits resume on their own.\n• BND-11 / BLD-06 / CAP-10 done: refinement v2 never falls below the algorithm on held-out data (22 of 22 formula files). Names used only where the data are silent: wrong names cost nothing, right names help in 1 of 10 families (R6 refuted). gpt-4o fenced most JSON replies, so the strict contract abstained on a third of the questions; 0 crashes.\n\n**Done** (5)\n• ✅ BLD-06 Drop-in replacement for Causal-Copilot's refinement stage\n• ✅ BND-11 LIVE: Refinement v2, names only where the data are silent\n• ✅ CAP-10 Robustness to malformed model output\n• ✅ RQ-17 Do results hold for a second model?\n• ✅ TGT-13 Zero crashes from malformed model output\n\n**Due in the next 14 days**\n• 2026-10-16 CRS-07 Decision gate G1\n• 2026-10-19 CRS-01 TA check-in 1 (TA: Nate)\n• 2026-10-20 BND-03 Paper and code audit: headline claims, methods text, untouched modules…\n• 2026-10-22 BND-02 Primary sources: literature re-reads, deep reads, method choices\n• 2026-10-24 BND-06 Remaining baselines, order sensitivity, scoreboard package (no LLM)\n• 2026-10-24 BND-08 LIVE: Causal-Copilot on CausalArena's named scenarios (old bundle 2)\n• 2026-10-28 BND-10 Refinement v1: held-out test\n\nTotals: ✅ 117 · 👀 17 · ⏳ 59 · 🔴 2 · 🔵 29",
